course: dictionary
lesson: 10427
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and troop is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. In «a troop of monkeys huddles together in the snow», the monkeys are not soldiers, so troop means a group of animals.
explain: Troop can also be a verb, an action word. «The children trooped into the hall» tells you they walked in together as a group, often in a line. The word trooped shows what they did.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «a troop of soldiers» fit? Yes. Does «a troop of scouts» fit? Also yes, because troop can mean any group of people or animals.
fact: Troop is a noun and a verb.
fact: «Troops» means soldiers, especially a large group of them.
fact: «A troop of monkeys» is a group of monkeys that live and move together.
fact: «Troop in» and «troop out» mean walking in or out together as a group.
exercise: «A troop of monkeys huddles together in the snow.» What is a troop here? | A pile of snow | *A group of animals | A kind of forest | A group of soldiers
exercise: «The children trooped into the hall.» What does trooped mean? | Sat down quietly | Shouted loudly | *Walked in together as a group | Ran out alone
exercise: «The troops were sent to help after the flood.» Which meaning of troops fits? | *Soldiers, especially a large group of them | Scouts on a camp | A type of pizza | Monkeys in the forest
test: «The scout troop went camping by the lake.» What does troop mean here? | A kind of tent | *A group of scouts | A group of soldiers | A lake
test: «Baboons live in big troops on the ground in Africa.» What is a troop in this sentence? | *A group of baboons living together | The ground in Africa | A safe place to sleep | Lions and leopards
exam: In «The soldiers trooped out of the tent», what does trooped mean? | Fell asleep | Ran away alone | Sang a song | *Walked out together as a group
